L001165	In summary, the first study of \VVH production through vector boson scattering is presented, using proton-proton collision data recorded by the CMS experiment at the LHC in 2016--2018, at $\sqrt{s} = 13\TeV$, corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 138\fbinv.
L001166	Selected events are consistent with the presence of two jets originating from VBS and an \PH decaying into a pair of \PQb quarks, reconstructed as a single large-radius jet.
L001167	Final states with zero, one, or two charged leptons arising from the decay of two vector bosons are studied.
L001168	The VBS \VVH production is excluded at 95\%~\CL for values of the \kVV coupling modifier outside the observed (expected) range of $0.40 < \kVV < 1.60$ ($0.34 < \kVV < 1.66$), assuming all other \PH couplings are equal to their values in the standard model.
L001169	The results represent one of the best constraints to date on \kVV using CMS data, complementing the results obtained from searches for \PH pair production, and laying the foundation for future, similar studies.
L001170	The \kWW and \kZZ coupling modifiers are also constrained independently in the observed (expected) ranges of $0.17 < \kWW < 1.84$ ($0.11 < \kWW < 1.89$) and $-0.37 < \kZZ < 2.38$ ($-0.54 < \kZZ < 2.54$), respectively.
L001171	A two-dimensional scan, determining exclusion regions in the \kWW-\kZZ plane, is also provided, which largely improves on the constraints coming from the CMS search for $\PV\PH\PH$ production.
