L001183	This section details the event selections used in each channel before multivariate analyses are performed.
L001184	In the all-hadronic channels, events of interest are collected using triggers based on $H_\mathrm{T}$, with thresholds of 800 or 900\GeV for 2016, and 1050\GeV for 2017 and 2018.
L001185	Events must contain at least two AK8 jets with $\pt > 300\GeV$, and $\pt > 550$\GeV for the leading one to ensure full trigger efficiency.
L001186	Two categories are defined to distinguish fully and semi-boosted events.
L001187	In the fully boosted channel, the \Htobb candidate is selected as the AK8 jet with the highest \Xtobb \ParticleNet score ($>0.5$), and the vector boson candidates are selected as the two highest \pt remaining AK8 jets with \Xtoqq scores $>0.3$.
L001188	In the semi-boosted channel, exactly two AK8 jets are required.
L001189	The \Htobb candidate is selected as the AK8 jet with the highest \Xtobb score ($>0.8$).
L001190	One of the two vector bosons is reconstructed as the other AK8 jet in the event, requiring an \Xtoqq minimum score of 0.637, 0.579, and 0.59 for 2016, 2017, and 2018 data taking, respectively.
L001191	The second vector boson is reconstructed from two AK4 jets ($\pt > 20$\GeV, $\abs{\eta}<2.5$) chosen as the closest pair in $\Delta R$. Two AK4 VBS jet candidates are also required.
L001192	In the case of multiple pairs, the one with the largest \absdetajj is selected as the VBS jet pair.
