L001400	\subsection{Signal region definition}
L001401	\label{endmatter:mvaanalysis}
L001402	
L001403	After the event selection, a multivariate analysis is performed in all channels.
L001404	In the all-hadronic, single-lepton and OS dilepton channels, an ``ABCD'' method~\cite{CDF:1990kbl} is used: the signal region, or region A, is defined alongside orthogonal control regions B, C, and D, used to predict the background in region A from data.
L001405	The selections used in each channel to define the signal region, or region A, are summarized in Table~\ref{tab:SRs}.
L001406	The ``AC axis'' selection, relying on the properties of the \VVH system, is inverted to define the region C; the ``AB axis'' selection, using the properties of the VBS jets, is inverted to define the region B; both are inverted to define the region D.
L001407	Additional selections, depending on the channel, are applied after the training of the discriminators to further improve the sensitivity of the search, and are common to the regions A, B, C and D.
L001408	These selections are applied only after the training in order to preserve the statistical power of the simulated samples at training time.
L001409	They are limited to the \ParticleNet \Xtobb and \Xtoqq scores, which are largely independent of the global event kinematic properties.
L001410	
L001411	In the SS dilepton channel, a BDT is also trained to discriminate signal from background, and the signal region is divided into three bins according to the BDT output score ($\left[0, 0.1\right]$, $\left[0.1, 0.25\right]$, $\left[0.25, 1\right]$).
